 of reflective  writing every week  so i think the way it's different is  just it has to be really sequential  for people to follow clearly does that  answer your question sure  and i can comment on taking an online  one although i haven't taken it  live so i can't compare but one thing  that came to my mind was how we have to  spend so much  of our time here at cornell in the stuff  that we are good at or supposed to be  good at  or you know like the things that we have  spent time  preparing for and for me not knowing  anything about  art and going into this just the basics  just the basics  reading the book that marcia referred to  it was like oh who knew  you know just so i was reminded of  him a children's quote about the expert  mind has very few  possibilities but the beginner's mind  has lots of possibilities  and so that's part of what it did for me  thanks  any other comments or questions  there are six handouts i didn't make  tons of copies because i didn't know  everyone would want them but there are  there's  there's a participation rubric that i  just love  it defines what participation is in my  classes and there's some reflective  writing guidelines  and rubrics there's a final project  guidelines  and then there's that upside down  drawing so that does give you a little  window into that  part and i again i know that i've taken  one part of my work and bond  into a deeply but if you ever have any  other questions about  you know that first jam-packed set of  slides if you're curious about or you  see opportunities for collaboration or  something then  don't hesitate to speak up so thank you  for being attentive  this has been a production of cornell  university  on the web at cornell.edu  you


